cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or results, please cite it as below."
title: "Testing the Transparency–Competition Premise: Evidence from EU Public Procurement"
abstract: >-
  Three quasi-experimental designs on the complete EU Tenders Electronic Daily
  record (EU-28, 2013–2023) test whether mandatory e-procurement disclosure
  raises competition: a staggered-adoption group-time ATT, a contract-level
  fixed-effects panel with dose-response, and a sharp regression discontinuity
  at the legal procurement threshold — the main design, re-specified on the
  pre-award statutory estimate that the law actually uses. All three converge on
  a null for competition intensity (main estimate −0.67 pp on the single-offer
  share, 95% CI [−3.66, +2.32], n = 179,065), with one surviving finding on
  participation (a strong cross-country association between digital depth and
  the SME share of tenders) and one threshold-regime result on the foreign-winner
  share. The repository ships the full audit trail: six design versions, the
  frozen pre-registration with its correction addendum, a 16-record failure log,
  and 556 automated checks of every number in the paper.
authors:
  - name: "NEO Research Program"
date-released: "2026-10-25"
version: "2.0"
url: "https://github.com/TSUBARAYA/procurement-disclosure-null"
